  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "16029700",
      "title": "Adding, Modifying & Deleting Properties",
      "lectureOrder": 216,
      "videoOrder": 188,
      "sourceHash": "e6140ec11a746dd5572a57a4134f23277fa00e6af6b0725a5457329cf7b435fa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "So our basic object here, of course, works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 6.03,
          "en": "Now let's say we created an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.03,
          "end": 8.37,
          "en": "and then for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.37,
          "end": 10.5,
          "en": "maybe because a user clicked a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.5,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "and that triggers that we want to edit this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "we want to add a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 18.03,
          "en": "after this object has been created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 19.92,
          "en": "Now, there are two approaches.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.92,
          "end": 22.02,
          "en": "The more complex approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.02,
          "end": 24.39,
          "en": "would be to create a brand new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.39,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "For this, we would have to turn this into a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "so that we can assign a new value to person",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 31.5,
          "en": "because with a const, this would not be allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.5,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "If you have a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.64,
          "en": "you must not ever assign a new value to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.64,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "with the equal sign.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 41.76,
          "en": "And then we could recreate this object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 44.16,
          "en": "Now we can copy over everything from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.16,
          "end": 47.34,
          "en": "and, of course, then add whatever we want to add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.34,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "Let's say isAdmin: true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "Now, of course, that's super complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "and not really what we might wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "Also, if we changed some value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.89,
          "en": "we have to ensure that we pick up any changes that were made",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.89,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "between this declaration and this reassignment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.23,
          "en": "so in some code in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 64.23,
          "end": 66.54,
          "en": "So this is typically not what we might wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 66.54,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "in most use cases",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.55,
          "en": "and certainly not manually by copying all the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.55,
          "end": 75.21000000000001,
          "en": "Instead, what you can always do on JavaScript objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.21000000000001,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "is you can use the dot notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 80.94,
          "en": "and simply access a property which you haven't added before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.94,
          "end": 82.8,
          "en": "For example, isAdmin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "At this point of time, person has no isAdmin property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 89.4,
          "en": "We didn't add it here, but you can do this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 89.4,
          "end": 93.66,
          "en": "Now if you try to log this, you'll also not get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 93.66,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "and I'll remove that greet function call here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 98.00999999999999,
          "en": "so that this alert doesn't always open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 98.00999999999999,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "So if you log that, we won't get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "Instead, we just log undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "That's also something to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.03999999999999,
          "en": "If you access a property on an object which doesn't exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 107.03999999999999,
          "end": 108.63,
          "en": "you're not getting an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 108.63,
          "end": 110.85,
          "en": "Instead, you get undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 110.85,
          "end": 113.34,
          "en": "But what you can do is you can simply assign a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 113.34,
          "end": 117.39,
          "en": "to this property now even if you didn't define it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 120.24,
          "en": "You can simply set this to true and if you thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 120.24,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "console.log your entire person, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 126.18,
          "en": "you'll see that isAdmin is now a part of that person.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 126.18,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "So if we reload this and expand it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 130.56,
          "en": "we see isAdmin has been added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 130.56,
          "end": 133.14,
          "en": "So adding properties on the fly is super easy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 135.48,
          "en": "You just access them with the dot notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 135.48,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "and assign a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 139.07999999999998,
          "en": "And it doesn't matter if that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 139.07999999999998,
          "end": 140.85,
          "en": "was part before or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 140.85,
          "end": 143.31,
          "en": "If it wasn't part of the person before, it's now added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 143.31,
          "end": 144.36,
          "en": "If it was part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 144.36,
          "end": 147.9,
          "en": "so if you would set person.age to 31, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 150.27,
          "en": "well then we, of course, override that old value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 150.27,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "So we either override or we add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "and both works, both is supported,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 158.16,
          "en": "and that, of course, gives us a lot of flexibility there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 158.16,
          "end": 159.12,
          "en": "Now sometimes you also want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 159.12,
          "end": 161.16,
          "en": "to get rid of a certain property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 161.16,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "Let's say you want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 165.75,
          "en": "that you actually delete the age here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 165.75,
          "end": 167.46,
          "en": "So instead of reassigning it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 167.46,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "we want to get rid of a property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "That's also possible with a special keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 175.47,
          "en": "JavaScript provides to you, the delete keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.47,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "You just type delete like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 180.96,
          "en": "then a wide space so that this is a standalone keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 180.96,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "and then simply person dot and then whatever property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "you want to delete, for example age, just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.53,
          "en": "And this will delete the age property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 190.53,
          "end": 192.153,
          "en": "from the person object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 193.2,
          "end": 195.66,
          "en": "So if we now save that and we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 199.11,
          "en": "you will see that in the log, person.age is missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 199.11,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "So if you ever want to remove a property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 203.61,
          "en": "that is one way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 203.61,
          "end": 206.97,
          "en": "Now, always keep in mind if we thereafter try to access age,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 206.97,
          "end": 209.88,
          "en": "we'll not get an error, we'll just get undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 209.88,
          "end": 211.56,
          "en": "So deleting a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 211.56,
          "end": 214.98,
          "en": "is basically as if you would set it to undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 214.98,
          "end": 218.07,
          "en": "So if I reload here, we see undefined gets logged here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 218.07,
          "end": 220.89,
          "en": "Therefore, another way of getting rid of a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 220.89,
          "end": 223.56,
          "en": "is to use person.age in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 223.56,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "so instead of using this, and setting it equal to undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.65,
          "en": "Now, this is not super clean though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 229.65,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "It will work, it will do the trick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "and you can technically use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "but it is a good rule to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 238.14,
          "en": "that you should actually never assign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 240.42,
          "en": "undefined to any value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 240.42,
          "end": 242.31,
          "en": "You might remember earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 242.31,
          "end": 245.01,
          "en": "I mentioned that we have undefined and null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 248.37,
          "en": "Null is the value we use if we want to reset something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 248.37,
          "end": 250.35,
          "en": "if we want to clear something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 250.35,
          "end": 253.2,
          "en": "Undefined is a value which we as a developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 253.2,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "never actively assign to anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 259.05,
          "en": "Instead, undefined just is a default value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 259.05,
          "end": 262.5,
          "en": "JavaScript assigns to uninitialized variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 262.5,
          "end": 264.33,
          "en": "or properties in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "So doing this technically works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 267.21,
          "en": "and you can do it, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 267.21,
          "end": 270.33,
          "en": "It's not a hard rule that you should never assign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 270.33,
          "end": 273.09000000000003,
          "en": "undefined to anything, but you might consider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 273.09000000000003,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "if you really wanna do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "This here might be cleaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 279.65999999999997,
          "en": "It clearly expresses what you wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 279.65999999999997,
          "end": 282.45,
          "en": "The effect here is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 282.45,
          "end": 284.94,
          "en": "Now, you would, by the way, not have the same effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 284.94,
          "end": 287.58,
          "en": "if you would set person.age to null.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 287.58,
          "end": 288.72,
          "en": "This will reset it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 288.72,
          "end": 291.87,
          "en": "but what you'll see is that if you now reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 291.87,
          "end": 295.62,
          "en": "we log null here, and if I log the entire person,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 295.62,
          "end": 296.453,
          "en": "you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 297.69,
          "end": 300.93,
          "en": "that age is now still an active property of person,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 300.93,
          "end": 304.2,
          "en": "so to say, because null is not exactly the same as undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 304.2,
          "end": 305.13,
          "en": "as you also learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 305.13,
          "end": 306.75,
          "en": "It's not exactly the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 306.75,
          "end": 309.12,
          "en": "They are of different types in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 309.12,
          "end": 310.53,
          "en": "and therefore, it's a difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 310.53,
          "end": 311.94,
          "en": "if you set something to null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 311.94,
          "end": 315.45,
          "en": "which really just means the person has this property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 315.45,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "we just don't have a value in there right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 319.17,
          "en": "Or if you set it to undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 319.17,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "which means this person doesn't even have an age property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 324.99,
          "en": "And important, setting it to undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 324.99,
          "end": 327.48,
          "en": "means it doesn't have age property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 327.48,
          "end": 331.38,
          "en": "Technically, if you console.log the entire person,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 331.38,
          "end": 334.53,
          "en": "no matter if you set age to null or undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
